// Array-literal arguments to imported functions with narrow element types. The
// imported-call path used to skip the element hint and narrowing that local
// calls get, so the literal's elements stayed 64-bit and the JIT read them at
// the parameter's width — silently wrong: asum printed 201, asecond 0 and
// athird 0.
#![imports]
m: use "./t_import_array_literal_arg_lib"

print(m.asum([1, 2, 3]))
print(m.asecond([300, 9]))
print(m.athird([1, 2, 3]))
